 ],
 "literal": "She became like this, she of the beautiful forehead, saying to him / approaching and going, those who would speak, if we obtain / it would be good indeed, may you live, friend, in our garden / where water flows, in the green bushes, flourished / rain-time sponge gourd's blossoms, some, taking.",
 "translation": "O friend, may you live long! If only we could find messengers who would go to him, approach him, and say, 'She of the beautiful forehead has become like this,' taking with them a few blossoms of the sponge gourd that have flourished in the wet, green bushes of our garden during the rains, it would be so good indeed!",
 "modern": "தோழியே, நீ வாழ்க! நம் வீட்டுத் தோட்டத்து ஈரமான பசுமையான புதர்களில் மழைக் காலத்தில் செழித்து மலர்ந்த பீர்க்கம்பூக்கள் சிலவற்றை எடுத்துக் கொண்டு, அவரிடம் சென்று, 'அழகிய நெற்றியை உடையவள் இவ்வாறு மெலிந்து போனாள்' என்று சொல்லக்கூடிய தூதுவர்களைப் பெற்றால் எவ்வளவு நன்றாக இருக்கும்!",
 "explanation": "The heroine is speaking to her friend during the rainy season, which is the time the hero promised to return from his journey. Seeing the sponge gourd flowers blooming in her garden, which are yellow and symbolize her own paleness caused by separation, she feels deep grief. She wishes she could find messengers who would go to the hero and show him these flowers as proof of her suffering. The yellow blossoms of the sponge gourd represent the yellow-green pallor of pacaḷai that spreads over her skin due to her longing. Key words include 'பீரம்' (sponge gourd), 'அலர்' (blossoms), 'இன்னளாயினள்' (she became like this), and 'நன்னுதல்' (beautiful forehead).",
